          against property title. Where most damaged houses have no registered title,
          that substitution is the only thing that makes a per-household payment
          possible at all -- and it is the single most transferable design idea in
          this whole file."}
  :instrument/household-grant {:en "Cash grant disbursed through the national social-protection payment rail"
                               :note "Using an existing cash-transfer system rather than building a disaster one
                                      collapses the entitlement queue from months to weeks, because the identity,
                                      eligibility and payment plumbing already exist and are already audited."}
  :instrument/emergency-repair {:en "Materials and cash-for-shelter through humanitarian shelter cluster partners"}
  :instrument/public-demolition {:en "Not a programme. Damaged mud-built housing is cleared by the household."}
  :instrument/business-grant {:en "Agricultural input packages (seed, fertiliser, livestock) rather than business grants"
                              :note "For a mostly agricultural affected population the livelihood instrument is the
                                     next planting season, and it has a hard meteorological deadline."}
  :instrument/insurance {:en "Effectively absent for households" :status :unverified-in-repo}
  :instrument/volunteer-coordination {:en "Humanitarian cluster system, military engineering, and local philanthropic networks"}
  :instrument/waste-plan {:en "No formal disaster-waste stream; mud-built structures largely return to the ground"
